<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlos Montúfar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1780">1780</a>–<a href="/years/1816">1816</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Carlos de Montúfar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlos Montúfar was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> aristocrat and soldier, son of the Marquis of Selva Alegre. Sent to Quito in 1810 as a royal commissioner of the Regency, he sided with the patriots and promoted the second junta. He commanded its forces against the royalists, later fought for independence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a> and was executed by the Spanish in 1816.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carlos-montufar.jpg" alt="Carlos Montúfar" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manuel Salas Alzamora · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carlos_de_Mont%C3%BAfar_y_Larrea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
